Project: chunkvault, a distributed file storage system in C++20 using CMake, vcpkg, Drogon, PostgreSQL, Redis.

Code style:
- Modern C++20, RAII, smart pointers, no raw owning pointers. Follow the Google C++ style with clang-format.
- Comments only where the reason is not obvious. No comments that restate the code.
- No emojis anywhere (code, logs, docs, commit messages).
- No placeholder text such as "TODO: implement" or tutorial-style example blocks.
- Use clear domain names (ChunkStore, ReplicaManager), not generic ones (Helper, Utils).

Engineering rules:
- Configuration from environment variables or a config file, never hardcoded. No secrets in the repo.
- Layers: api (controllers), services (business logic), repositories (DB access), models.
- Every feature ships with GoogleTest unit tests under tests/.
- Explicit error handling, correct HTTP status codes, structured logging with spdlog.
- Small, focused changes. Do not modify unrelated files.